1
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,548
The MoU trap. Episode 6. Closing the trap

2
00:00:11,598 --> 00:00:15,225
An MoU checked against the plan before signature,

3
00:00:15,775 --> 00:00:18,463
with milestones and a sunset date,

4
00:00:19,013 --> 00:00:22,447
reviewed by the utility and the ministry of finance,

5
00:00:22,997 --> 00:00:24,085
and published,

6
00:00:24,635 --> 00:00:27,878
is no longer a trap. It is a development tool.

7
00:00:31,028 --> 00:00:34,335
The trap has five costs. Power not delivered.

8
00:00:34,885 --> 00:00:36,549
Better projects blocked.

9
00:00:37,099 --> 00:00:39,701
Scarce public attention consumed.

10
00:00:40,251 --> 00:00:43,622
Credibility lost when signed terms are reopened.

11
00:00:44,172 --> 00:00:48,609
And liabilities created when trapped projects close under pressure.

12
00:00:50,809 --> 00:00:53,625
Bring the cost, and the risk bearers, forward.

13
00:00:54,125 --> 00:01:00,674
Filter at entry: no MoU outside the least-cost plan unless it has been tested against the plan.

14
00:01:01,224 --> 00:01:05,896
Price the option, with securities, milestones and sunset clauses.

15
00:01:06,446 --> 00:01:15,492
Bring the risk bearers in early: the utility and the ministry of finance review any MoU that could lead to fixed payments or state support.

16
00:01:16,042 --> 00:01:20,074
And publish a register of power MoUs and their status.

17
00:01:22,274 --> 00:01:33,069
Nigeria shows that pricing the option is not enough on its own. Securities were posted, and the projects still stalled, on the tariff, the buyer and state support.

18
00:01:34,169 --> 00:01:38,414
The trap has to be closed at every point where a project is tested.

19
00:01:40,964 --> 00:01:45,401
Hence the Sustainable Financial Close Test proposed in the book.

20
00:01:46,701 --> 00:01:55,299
A power deal closes only when both the lender's test and the state's test have been passed, and the state's answer has been made public.

21
00:01:57,849 --> 00:02:00,260
Next episode: Before you sign.
